                    {
                        "form_id": "4fb560ad-b537-4543-a374-42ab6535831d",
                        "entry_id": "fac0de74-5f41-3fb9-bc8a-f80d8facbcb7",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "carminatives"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "68ad28d1-b68a-3019-bff6-96f9ebe2b8c8",
                        "entry_id": "fac0de74-5f41-3fb9-bc8a-f80d8facbcb7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui favorise l’expulsion des flatuosités contenues dans l’intestin, en parlant des substances médicinales."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cdc3b7f-d36b-4c0c-998d-4e682a4b11c7",
                                "sense_id": "68ad28d1-b68a-3019-bff6-96f9ebe2b8c8",
                                "text": "C’est sur ces bases étiologiques, qu’il était nécessaire, indiquer préalablement, que nous pouvons maintenant édifier la médication carminative."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b16831c5-6733-4652-a1de-ece4497e80f4",
                        "source_entry_id": "fac0de74-5f41-3fb9-bc8a-f80d8facbcb7",
                        "source_sense_id": "68ad28d1-b68a-3019-bff6-96f9ebe2b8c8",
                        "target_lang_word": "carminative",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "carminative",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "749f1933-f8d2-382a-8056-ce1be1749ab9",
                                        "entry_id": "746866cb-30e1-3828-bc18-9828b666f80d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relieving the discomfort of gas in the digestive tract, either by reducing its production (by the gut microbiota) or by inducing its expulsion (whether as belches [upper GI action] or as flatus [lower GI action])."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd830553-9768-4a68-9817-ff2df297e019",
                                                "sense_id": "749f1933-f8d2-382a-8056-ce1be1749ab9",
                                                "text": "If too much milke be the cauſe, then the Nurſe ſhall not give the childe ſucke ſo often, nor in ſuch plenty: If it proceed from wind, and that doe cauſe the childe to be thus troubled, it ſhall be diſcuſſed with Fomentations applied to the belly and navell; and with Carminative Cliſters, which ſhall bee given him, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4378bd0c-2b12-4567-93dd-55f2143c8892",
                                                "sense_id": "749f1933-f8d2-382a-8056-ce1be1749ab9",
                                                "text": "They used to give me cinnamon when I had a cold—quite useless, but not disagreeable. […] On the label was a list of its virtues, and among other things it was described as being in the highest degree carminative. I adored the word."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "carminative",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dee9e343-1b0c-370d-b7da-46bdd1512294",
                                        "entry_id": "7e03a351-6707-3a47-bb1a-3021e584e608",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A drug or substance that relieves the discomfort of gas in the digestive tract, either by reducing its production (by the gut microbiota) or by inducing its expulsion (whether as belches [upper GI action] or as flatus [lower GI action])."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b1a5da0-f44d-435e-8607-471723e50d9c",
                                                "sense_id": "dee9e343-1b0c-370d-b7da-46bdd1512294",
                                                "text": "“A mental carminative,” said Mr. Scogan reflectively. “That's what you need.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52eddd18-2941-45b2-b9f3-1e74451d8c0f",
                                                "sense_id": "dee9e343-1b0c-370d-b7da-46bdd1512294",
                                                "text": "But Master Nathaniel was indifferent to these manifestations of unpopularity. Let mental suffering be intense enough, and it becomes a sort of carminative."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0ffab07d-18ce-45ce-b332-31a8a93f1811",
                        "source_entry_id": "fac0de74-5f41-3fb9-bc8a-f80d8facbcb7",
                        "source_sense_id": "68ad28d1-b68a-3019-bff6-96f9ebe2b8c8",
